# M5.4 acceptance: tool activity lines and the permission dialog, against a
# fake sidecar (no Claude calls). Run from the worktree root:
#
#   P=$(mktemp -d)                     # scratch project folder
#   H=$(mktemp -d)                     # isolated HOME for config and logs
#   cp tests/data/sample.pdf "$P/"
#   READER_SIDECAR_CMD="sh $PWD/tests/acceptance/m5.4-fake-sidecar.sh" \
#     scripts/shot.sh -o <repo>/.verify/m5.4/<impl|review|tester> \
#     -s tests/acceptance/m5.4.steps -- \
#     env HOME="$H" ./build/app/agentic-reader "$P/sample.pdf"
#
# Then, after shot.sh exits 0:
#   grep -q "introduces the Transformer" "$P/notes.md"       # must succeed
#   L=$(find "$H" -name sidecar.log)
#   grep -o 'fake: {.*"type":"permission_reply".*' "$L"
# The last command must print exactly three lines, in this order, with
# "allow":false, "allow":false, "allow":true (Return, Escape, Alt+A below).
# A request that is already over (timed out, chat lost, sidecar restarted)
# gets no reply, so no fourth line. A fourth line naming the crash case's
# req_id breaks spec 4 ("close the dialog without replying").
#
# Never run this with the PDF in tests/data: the fake writes notes.md into the
# project folder, which is the folder of the open PDF.
#
# tests/acceptance/m5.4-fake-sidecar.sh documents the fake. In short, by
# prompt text, each message 0.3 s apart:
#   "tools"     text, one tool_use per formatted tool (Read, Glob, Grep,
#               Write, Edit, Bash, WebFetch, WebSearch) plus an unknown tool
#               mcp__notes__save, then result. About 4 s.
#   "notes.md"  tool_use Write, then permission_request Write for
#               <project>/notes.md, then waits for the reply. It reports the
#               reply it got ("Permission reply: allow|deny.") and whether
#               the file exists on disk ("notes.md exists: yes|no.").
#   "timeout"   permission_request Bash "rm -rf build"; with no reply after
#               4 s, "No answer, so the tool was denied." and result.
#   "lost"      permission_request Bash "make install"; with no reply after
#               4 s, error kind process ("simulated CLI exit, the chat is
#               closed").
#   "crash"     permission_request Bash "git push"; 4 s later the fake kills
#               itself and the app restarts it.
#   otherwise   "OK." and result.
# A permission_reply for a req_id the running fake never sent (such as one
# sent to the restarted fake for a request from before the crash) comes back
# as an error "unexpected permission_reply <req_id>", a red notice. That text
# must not appear in any shot.
#
# Layout (same as m5.2.steps): 1400x900 window at the screen origin, chat
# pane x 980..1400, message input at about (1180, 800).
#
# Assumptions the steps rely on (the spec is silent):
#   - PermissionDialog has two buttons labelled "&Allow" and "&Deny", so
#     Alt+A presses Allow.
#   - Deny is the default button and has keyboard focus when the dialog
#     opens, so Return presses Deny.
#   - The dialog is centred on the frame and does not cover the chat input.
#   - Tool lines are plain text in a smaller grey font, one line per tool_use,
#     placed in the reply where the tool_use arrived (between the text
#     before and after it).
wait 3

click 1180 800
type show tools
key Return
wait 6

# Tool activity. Under the user message "show tools" the reply reads "Let me
# look through the project first." followed by three grey lines, one per
# tool, then "Found the section. Now a draft and some checks." followed by
# six more grey lines, then "That is everything I needed." and the grey cost
# line. The nine tool lines, each on a single line, in a grey (dimmer,
# smaller or both) font unlike the reply text:
#   Read papers/attention.pdf pages 10-12        (exactly this)
#   Glob ... **/*.pdf
#   Grep ... softmax ... papers
#   Write notes/draft.md                          (no "DRAFT-BODY")
#   Edit notes/draft.md                           (no "OLD-TEXT" or "NEW-TEXT")
#   Bash grep -c "<b>" notes.md && wc -l notes.md (the angle brackets, quotes
#                                                  and "&&" shown literally,
#                                                  nothing bold)
#   WebFetch https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762     (no "PROMPT-TEXT")
#   WebSearch ... transformer positional encoding
#   mcp__notes__save {"tags":["a","b"],"title":"Draft"}
# No raw "tool_use" or other unformatted JSON besides the last line. Send is
# enabled and Stop greyed out. No red notice.
shot tool-lines

click 1180 800
type Please write a summary to notes.md
key Return
wait 2.5

# The permission dialog is open over the main window, modal. It names the
# tool "Write" and shows the formatted input: the full path
# <scratch folder>/notes.md and the content "# Summary" and "The paper
# introduces the Transformer." It has an Allow and a Deny button, with Deny
# marked as the default (focus ring or default-button style). Behind it the
# chat shows "I will save a short summary." and a grey line
# "Write <scratch folder>/notes.md". Stop is enabled (the reply is running).
shot permission-dialog

click 1180 800
type zzz
wait 1

# Still modal: the click on the chat input and the typing did not reach the
# main window. The dialog is still open and unchanged, and the chat input
# behind it is empty (no "zzz").
shot dialog-is-modal

key Return
wait 2

# Return pressed the default button, Deny. The dialog is closed. The reply
# continues under the grey Write line: "Permission reply: deny." then
# "notes.md exists: no." then the grey cost line. The chat input is empty.
shot denied-by-return

click 1180 800
type Write it to notes.md again
key Return
wait 2.5
key Escape
wait 2

# Escape denied. The dialog is closed. A second user message "Write it to
# notes.md again" whose reply ends "Permission reply: deny." and
# "notes.md exists: no." with the grey cost line under it.
shot denied-by-escape

click 1180 800
type Now really write notes.md
key Return
wait 2.5
key alt+a
wait 2

# Allow. The dialog is closed. A third user message "Now really write
# notes.md" whose reply ends "Permission reply: allow." and
# "notes.md exists: yes." with the grey cost line under it.
shot allowed

click 1180 800
type Try the timeout case
key Return
wait 2.5

# The permission dialog is open again, now for tool "Bash" with the command
# "rm -rf build". Behind it the chat shows "I want to clean the build
# folder." and a grey line "Bash rm -rf build".
shot stale-dialog-open

wait 5

# Nobody answered. The fake gave up and ended the reply with `result`, so
# the stale dialog closed by itself. The reply reads "No answer, so the tool
# was denied." and ends with the grey cost line. Send is enabled and Stop
# greyed out. No dialog is open.
shot stale-dialog-closed-by-result

click 1180 800
type Now the lost case
key Return
wait 8

# The dialog for Bash "make install" opened and then closed by itself when
# the reply ended with an error. The reply shows "I want to install the
# package.", a grey line "Bash make install", and a red notice containing
# "simulated CLI exit, the chat is closed" (with M5.2's note that the chat
# was reopened). No dialog is open. Send is enabled.
shot stale-dialog-closed-by-error

click 1180 800
type Finally the crash case
key Return
wait 2.5

# The permission dialog is open for tool "Bash" with the command
# "git push". Behind it the chat shows "I want to push the branch." and a
# grey line "Bash git push".
shot crash-dialog-open

wait 8

# The sidecar died while the dialog was open and has restarted. The dialog
# closed by itself without a reply. The chat shows M5.2's red notice that
# the assistant stopped unexpectedly and is restarting. No red notice
# containing "unexpected permission_reply" (that would mean the app answered
# the old request). No dialog is open. Send is enabled.
shot crash-dialog-closed

click 1180 800
type hello after the restart
key Return
wait 2

# The chat works after the restart: the user message "hello after the
# restart" and the reply "OK." with its grey cost line. Still no
# "unexpected permission_reply" notice anywhere in view. No dialog is open.
shot after-restart
